#
#   = <name>
#   f <file, repo-relative>
#   t <test names, space separated, without the .t>
#   - <the exact line to remove>
#   + <the line to put in its place; omit the line entirely to just delete>
#   m <optional: a fragment the failure MUST mention>
#
# Matching is EXACT, whole-line, and the target must be UNIQUE in the file: no
# regex, no delimiters, nothing to clash with the `||`, `*`, `$` and trailing
# backslashes these lines are full of. An absent line is a hard error, and so is
# an ambiguous one.
#
# `m` is what makes `killed` mean killed BY THE INTENDED ASSERTION. Without it,
# a mutation that happens to break an earlier, unrelated check counts as
# coverage. That is not hypothetical; see the fourth bullet above.
#
